+# tasklite package
+
+CLI (`cli.py`), HTTP API (`api.py`) and JSON-file storage (`store.py`). Both front ends go through `Store`.
+
+- Run CLI: `python3 -m tasklite add|list|done|stats`; API: `python3 -m tasklite.api` (127.0.0.1:8080).
+- Test (from repo root): `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. Offline, no setup.
+- Standard library only; keep it that way. Python 3.8+ syntax.
+
+## Gotchas
+- `DEFAULT_PATH` in `store.py` reads `TASKLITE_FILE` at import time; tests must pass an explicit `Store(path)`.
+- `Store.complete` raises `KeyError` on an unknown id; the API does not catch it.
+- A new CLI command needs a subparser and a branch in `cli.main`; a new API route goes in `api.do_GET`/`do_POST`.
+- Never commit `tasks.json` (gitignored user data).
